d3drm: viewport rendering, projection, picking, ray pick, ForceUpdate

Test test_sg_viewport_render (d3drm_test, 64+32): colours at pixels, half light, 60 degree light, depth order, wireframe, transforms, picking, ray picks, ForceUpdate. Gate fastb-gapdrm (runs d3drm_test); mutants DRM_LIGHT, PROJ, PICKSORT, FILL, FORCE shown caught. Conformance ours 64/32: 0 failures. GUESSED/unverified: lighting details (no lights = black ambient 0, two-sided normals, specular), default device quality (0 treated as GOURAUD), homogeneous layout of Transform, pick result conventions, ForceUpdate codes, mesh builder default colour 0 (Wine) renders as alpha 0 (invisible) until SetColor is called. Not done (no triage written, still open in gap-B): d3drm Clone methods, Save, mesh builder delete/optimize/submesh/enable/AddFrame/AddTriangles, d3drm GetDevices/GetNamedObject/EnumerateObjects/Tick/animation sets/shadows/user visuals/clipped visual/options/clients, device Init*/state change/win device, texture GenerateMIPMap, wrap Init/Apply, animation SetTime/DeleteKeyByID/ModifyKey, frame Load/GetHierarchyBox, viewport Clear DIRTYRECT. 
